        "student_prefix_sha256": "1d53ba1a1ed1c656d599c853775075abeb584fdd9d6ee5b4f5ea3ccb3442881e",
        "target": "Initially, there are 100 jelly beans in the bag. Out of 40 children, 80% were allowed to draw jelly beans. So, the number of children allowed to draw is 40 * 0.80 = 32 children. Each of these 32 children drew 2 jelly beans. Therefore, the total number of jelly beans drawn is 32 * 2 = 64 jelly beans. \n\nTo find out how many jelly beans remained in the bag, we subtract the total number of jelly beans drawn from the initial number of jelly beans: 100 - 64 = 36 jelly beans.\n\nFINAL: 36",
